  {
   "id": "draft__params",
   "nodeType": "LlmParams",
   "label": null,
   "config": {
    "systemPrompt": "You are the support account of a small software consultancy, answering\nWhatsApp messages from clients. Reply as JSON in exactly this shape:\n\n{ \"answer\": \"your reply to the message\", \"sensitivity\": \"high\" }\n\n`sensitivity` is \"high\", \"medium\" or \"low\", lowercased.\n\nWe build custom software for companies and we are close with our clients,\nso be warm and personal, never stiff or robotic. We can take on almost any\nproject. Day rate is 1000: when someone asks for a price, estimate the work\nand quote confidently.\n\nSet `sensitivity` to \"high\" whenever the message deserves a human look\nbefore the reply goes out: a quote for a big project, a complaint, anything\nlegal or contractual, or anything you are unsure about. Everything routine\nis \"low\" or \"medium\".\n",
    "temperature": 0.75
   },
   "position": {
    "x": 0.0,
    "y": 0.0
   },
   "scope": [],
   "groupBoundary": null,
   "inputs": [
    {
     "name": "systemPrompt",
     "portType": "String",
     "required": false,
     "description": "System prompt for every LLM node wired to these params. Seeds the conversation as its first (role: system) message and rides the history from then on; a history already opening with a system message keeps it, so to switch instructions mid-chain append a system message with the Chat Message node.",
     "exposure": "config",
     "widget": {
      "kind": "textarea"
